.TH voltkit-picker 1  "Voltkit 0.1.2" "Voltkit Manual"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
voltkit\-picker \- Open the snippet picker and paste the chosen snippet into the focused app
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBvoltkit picker\fR [\fB\-\-snippet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open the snippet picker and paste the chosen snippet into the focused app
.PP
Search with the keyboard, press Enter, and fill in any {arg:NAME} parameters. The expansion is pasted into the app that had focus, through the RemoteDesktop portal (the desktop asks for permission once), and the previous clipboard is restored.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-snippet\fR \fI<TRIGGER>\fR
Open directly on the snippet with this trigger
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH KEYS
.TP
\fBUp, Down\fR
Choose a snippet while typing in the search box.
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Insert the snippet, or move to the next parameter field.
.TP
\fBEscape\fR
Go back from the parameter form, or close the picker.
.SH NOTES
.PP
The first paste asks for remote\-desktop permission; the grant is remembered in ~/.local/state/voltkit/remote\-desktop\-token. If pasting is refused or unavailable, the expansion stays on the clipboard and a notification says to press Ctrl+V. Apps that paste with another shortcut, such as terminals, need paste_shortcut set in the [expander] section of the configuration.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Open the picker on one snippet\*(Aqs form:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBvoltkit picker \-\-snippet \*(Aq;quote\*(Aq\fR
.fi
.RE
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
